            <div xml:id="d88">

                <pb facs="0157" n="123" xml:id="pg123"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 88.</note>
                <head>Mr. E. B. Washburne to Mr. Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 297.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-09-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 30, 1870</date>. (Received October 18,
                        1870.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to send you herewith
                    copies of a correspondence between the consuls general and consuls of Southern
                    and Central America and myself, (including a letter from the minister of foreign
                    affairs,) in relation to my according the protection of the Government of the
                    United States to the arms, flags, residences, &amp;c., of their respective
                    consulates.</p>
                <closer><signed>E. B. WASHBURNE.</signed></closer>






